## Reference Implementation

The reference implementation of this protocol (`humanist-core`) is NOT part of this specification repository. 

The reference implementation is licensed separately under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (AGPLv3), with Commercial Dual Licensing available for enterprise deployments and closed-source embedding.

This deliberate separation ensures the protocol remains a vendor-neutral open standard, while the reference tooling, support, and enterprise integrations maintain a sustainable commercial model.

## Implementation Licensing Policy

The HACP project maintains a separate licensing policy for project-owned software implementations in Go, TypeScript, Python, and Rust.

The architectural policy and proposed licensing amendment are documented in:

- [Cross-Language Licensing Policy Decision](https://github.com/digital-humanism/hacp-spec/blob/docs/cross-language-licensing-policy/docs/licensing/HACP_CROSS_LANGUAGE_LICENSING_POLICY_DECISION_2026-10-09.md)
- [Cross-Language Licensing Amendment Package](https://github.com/digital-humanism/hacp-spec/blob/docs/cross-language-licensing-policy/docs/licensing/HACP_PHASE_B_LICENSING_AMENDMENT_PACKAGE_EN_2026-10-09.md)

These documents record an accepted policy and a proposed amendment, respectively. They do not themselves constitute an effective license grant.

The HACP specification and its normative materials remain licensed under CC BY 4.0. Existing license grants and applicable IETF rights remain unaffected.
